00:01:25.828 --> 00:01:27.855
(car body squeaking)

00:01:30.123 --> 00:01:31.540
- [Father] Is she asleep yet?

00:01:31.540 --> 00:01:33.490
- [Mother] Nope.

00:01:33.490 --> 00:01:34.767
- [Father] How 'bout now?

00:01:34.767 --> 00:01:36.299
- [Mother] No.

00:01:36.299 --> 00:01:36.973
- [Father] Now?

00:01:36.973 --> 00:01:39.532
- [Mother] No.

00:01:39.532 --> 00:01:40.913
I don't get it.

00:01:40.913 --> 00:01:44.455
I mean, I guess, let's
just let her stay up.

00:01:44.455 --> 00:01:45.940
- No.

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:47.876
I think I have one last thing.

00:01:49.866 --> 00:01:51.503
- What are you doing?

00:01:51.503 --> 00:01:55.101
- I read that if you do this,

00:01:55.101 --> 00:01:59.106
that they will asleep
in less than a minute.

00:01:59.106 --> 00:02:00.888
- Okay, we're trying to
get her to go asleep,

00:02:00.888 --> 00:02:03.436
not tease her like a southern belle.

00:02:07.575 --> 00:02:09.125
I stand corrected.

00:02:14.204 --> 00:02:16.094
(door creaking)

00:02:16.094 --> 00:02:18.659
(baby cooing)

00:02:18.659 --> 00:02:20.527
(frustrated sighing)

00:02:20.527 --> 00:02:22.256
- That's our bad.

00:02:22.256 --> 00:02:23.037
- Yeah.

